    <statement><p>Find <m>x</m> if <m>\displaystyle{\  \frac{(5)^x (5)^{6}}{(5)^{-3}}=(5)^{3} }</m></p>
<p><m>x =</m><fillin characters="3" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-6</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>Use properties of exponents to simplify the left side of the equation<m>\displaystyle{\begin{gathered} \frac{(5)^x (5)^{6}}{(5)^{-3}} = (5)^{3} \\
    (5)^x (5)^{6} (5)^{ + 3} = (5)^{3} \\
    (5)^{(x+6 + 3)} = (5)^{3}\ . \end{gathered} }</m> The two sides are equal if and only if the exponents are equal, so 
<m>\displaystyle{ x+6 + 3 = 3 }</m>. Solving for <m>x</m> one obtains <m>\displaystyle{ x = {-6} }</m>.</p>
</solution>
